    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: cd943fdaab0cce15aa6302ccc273fb39126396ea -->\n\nReview verdict: merge-ready (clean). This re-review ends the earlier change request on the head 04a91df1f. No blockers found.\n\nWhere this was built: locally in a fresh worktree at the head cd943fdaab0cce15aa6302ccc273fb39126396ea. This is a fork PR, so the pr-test.yml runner was not used (collaborator-only). Trial merge with origin/main: clean, no conflict (`git merge-tree --write-tree --messages origin/main cd943fdaa`, no conflict lines). The head is OPEN and not a draft.\n\nLocal results on the head (6 jobs, `cargo test` with 6 jobs, never -j 24):\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post --test linuxcnc_post` — pass, 5/5. The 3 pinning tests for #4151 (header clears G92.1 and states G97 by default, omits G92.1 when clearG92 is false, includes G92.1 when clearG92 is true) pass, and the 2 #4152 probe-guard tests pass. Binary: `crates/post/tests/linuxcnc_post.rs`.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test linuxcnc_post` — pass, 10/10. Previously 6/9 red; the allowlist (G92.1 and G97 added) and the exact header-line assertion now match the post output. Binary: `crates/app/tests/linuxcnc_post.rs`.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test conformance -- every_builtin_posts_every_golden_byte_exact the_synthesized_stream_locks_the_tool_and_spindle_words` — pass, 2/2. Byte-exact against the 13 regenerated goldens (12 LinuxCNC goldens plus synth_linuxcnc.nc): the regeneration really came from the post, not a hand edit.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` — clean, 0 warnings.\n\nChecks on the diff:\n- No new dependency between crates; no process file changed; no command added (post options are declared through the engine, not a user-facing command); no MCP tool needed.\n- The clearG92 boolean post property is declared (default true), read via optBool with a true fallback, and omitted only when set false; the empty word is filtered by the post's own block helper, so G97 is still emitted unconditionally.\n- The G92.1 and G97 words are emitted before the first spindle start, before the first traversal, and the header line is now \"G21 G17 G90 G91.1 G94 G40 G49 G80 G92.1 G97\". G92.1 clears any leftover G92 offset; G97 states constant-RPM mode; G97 is never written as a preamble companion, which matches the decision doc.\n- The goldens moved only in the header line, exactly 13 files, and the PR body lists them.\n- The decision doc records the dropped G92.1-in-preamble and G97-per-tool-change choices, and the cost to change later.\n- The PR body names the pinning tests and the goldens moved.\n\nResidual notes (not blocking):\n- G92.1 clears the G92 offsets; the control's work-offset words (G54..G59.3) are still written by the preamble, so the program is unaffected by a leftover G92 in any case.\n- Physical machine execution on LinuxCNC hardware was not exercised (not claimed in the PR body).\n\nThis review is a re-review of the changed head. The earlier request for changes (needs-rework + conflicts) is ended; merge-ready follows, and the maintainer approves and merges by hand.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
